  "problem": "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+5({y}^{2}+4y)+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5([y+2)^{2}-4]+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5(y+2)^{2}-20+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0).$",
